# T-1038: Calling builtin-pow without --- uses: produces a T002 warning.
#
# T002 is the type-checker's "undefined variable" warning (see `tinct explain T002`).
# builtin-* aliases live in the builtins_env baseline frame which is NOT exported
# into user-facing scope. Only --- uses: ["math"] injects them into document scope.
#
# The warning format is:
#   undefined variable: builtin-pow at SPAN
# This IS the T002 warning — the type checker cannot find builtin-pow in the
# type environment and emits "undefined variable" (T002 code).
#
# At runtime, the call still succeeds because the eval engine falls back to
# looking up builtin-pow in parent env frames. The warning is informational.
#
# See also: tests/corpus/eval/stdlib/uses_doc_isolation.llt-eval (WITH uses: ["core"])
#           tests/corpus/eval/builtins/pow.llt-eval (WITH uses: ["math"])
[builtin-pow 2 10]
=== out
Float(1024)
